our next guest is no stranger to  shattering glass ceilings cynthia  marshall became the first black female  ceo of an nba team in 2018. dallas  mavericks owner mark cuban hired her to  transform the team's toxic work culture  under marshall the mavericks leadership  team is now 50 women and 47 people of  color forbes has named her one of the  world's 15 most inspiring female leaders  and adweek called her one of the 30 most  powerful women in sports but here's the  thing she has broken barriers all her  life marshall was the first black  president in her high school and the  first black cheerleader at uc berkeley  and in her new book you've been chosen  thriving through the unexpected marshall  shares personal stories of resilience  that helped shape who she is today saint  marshall joins us right now good morning  how are you doing good morning i'm doing  fabulous how are you all doing great  thank you for joining us now you were  hired by mark cuban  to help change the culture now is this  true that at the time you didn't really  know much about basketball and if that's  the case then why did he feel like you  were the perfect person for the job and  he didn't know who mark cuban was okay  i'm a basketball fan but i didn't know  the business of basketball and i did not  know mark cuban so don't judge me i just  didn't but i know him now yeah i know  and he knows me yeah but i took it  because it was an opportunity uh to make  a difference and when mark laid out the  position and he was very sincere about  changing the culture i had done similar  work at at t which is how he got my name  and two women stopped me as i was  leaving his office and told me their  stories  and said you have to do this for us and  so i am you know i immediately said you  know let me go home and pray about it  because i pray about everything of  course and i came back and talked to the  employees the next day and for three  hours  i just heard different stories and i met  these wonderful people we have amazing  people at the dallas mavericks  and i said yes i said yes i said yes for  the sisterhood but it turned out to be  for  everybody and so it's been an amazing  experience with all these fabulous  people uh working to make a great place  to work i i don't take the credit for it  at all you've got the three principles  of leadership that you live by listen  learn and love do i have those rights  yes my three l's of leadership yes if i  to be an effective leader i need to  listen to the people and truly listen at  a very deep level listen to really  understand them i had one-on-ones with  every single maverick employee when i  got there and so to listen to the people  learn from the people i mean back in the  day i went to pole climbing school at  atnt just to learn you know what people  actually do every day so i could have  empathy for them and then to love them  to love them as people not as employees  but to love that person who gets up out  of bed in the morning that's who i want  to walk into our doors and so we have to  truly truly love them you know when mark  was here he was raving about you so i  really couldn't wait to meet you but  your book the the chosen is so  key i think to your life you had a very  abusive father who used to beat the crap  out of your mother you given vivid  detail broke your nose one time  you you talk about uh being diagnosed  with cancer colon cancer you survived  that you've had four miscarriages and  had a baby on the fifth time second  trimester miscarriages yes that baby  little carolyn did not live you've now  adopted uh four children but i also look  at what you've done in the corporate  world and this is what fascinated me  about the book early on in your career  you were told  uh do not wear braids take the braids  out of your hair do not wear red shoes  because they're not professional today  you're wearing hot pink shoes hot pink  that's really good you make it good man  you like these yeah yeah i'm making a  statement so that was early on sent yeah  and then later you get this big  promotion and you said that when she  called the person to give you the  promotion you could tell she wasn't  happy for you but what did she tell you  you needed to do in order to get the  promotion well she had left a magazine  on my desk so she told me that she  wanted me to look like the people on the  cover and so there were these black  people in all white  somebody had a short haircut so she  wanted me to cut my hair of course i  didn't want to do it my husband was in  the background saying i have a barber i  have a barber we can do this i'm like no  no this is she wants you to change your  name you want me to change my name so  she said i couldn't be sent because  nobody knows what ascent is i have to be  cindy or cynthia i can talk that loud i  can have all these people in my office  not laugh too loudly couldn't laugh too  loud she said i was just too happy and i  needed to be a little more stoic stop  saying the word blessed stop saying  blessed i need i stopped saying lucky  that i mean stop saying blessed that i  needed to say i was lucky so when  somebody tells you all of that scent  marshall when somebody tells you all of  that and you turned down the promotion  you turned down the progress you said  thanks but no thank you but when you've  gotten all these obstacles to overcome  what keeps you so enthusiastic and so  focused and so confident about what you  do well i think it's a it's a faith that  i have that i got from my mother uh that  no matter you know what happens uh it's  always going to come out better on the  other side and so and that's the what  the book is all about that i've been  chosen for this adversity we've all been  chosen uh for adversity but we're  uniquely a qualified to deal with it and  so it just uh it's a faith but and  knowing that i serve a purpose but you  were going to retire you were supposed  to retire when mark cuban called you you  have a four-year contract yes i was  retired and i started my own business  but i was called to do it i truly well  you know to do it we are glad that you  didn't retire sent marshall we  appreciate you thank you so much you've  been chosen on sale tomorrow and on  today's cbs morning's podcast saint  marshall shares the role that faith has  played in her professional and personal  life yeah thank you cindy thank you  thank you sister i like your green shoot  okay thank you very much
 

